      "problem": "Calculate the slope of the line that passes through the points $(1, 5)$ and $(4, 2).$",
      "worked_solution": "We let $(x_1,y_1) = (1,5)$ and $(x_2,y_2) = (4,2),$ and compute the slope using the formula:\n\n$$\n\\eqalign{\n\t\tm &= \\dfrac {y_2 - y_1} {x_2 - x_1} \\\n\t\t    &= \\dfrac {2 - 5} {4 - 1} \\\n\t\t    &= \\dfrac {-3}{3} \\\n\t\t    &= -1\n\t}\n$$\n\nThus, the slope is $m=-1.$",
